notes.content:
Dear Warriors! Another year has passed, and we are thrilled to begin the celebration of the 17th Anniversary of the world of Elinor!

Until the end of April, Zlatovan and Koragor are waiting for your participation in the festive quests “Honor and Respect,” “Holiday Chores,” and “Festive Treat". They are also ready to gift you the Holiday Chest XVII!
Iria and Kragor will join you in baking the "Best Cake Ever" until April 30th inclusive. You have until June 30th to bake it and enjoy its festive bonus.
By defeating experienced monsters until April 20th inclusive, you have a chance to find collectible coins (17c, 17s, and 17g) among your other trophies. Coins from past years' collections can be purchased in the Crystal Store.
Additionally, you can unlock a new festive achievement -  Fireworks IV”!

Throughout the week, special discounts will apply across Technomagic:
- 50% off clan and artifact armor and jewelry in stores;
- 50% off crafting equipment in the in-game forge (without exchange!);
- 50% off skins and avatars in the Artifact Hall, Secretariat, and the Season Store;
- 50% off all medals for sale;
- 40% off ingredients and tools in city stores and clan laboratories;
- 30% off Assistant's Chest;
- 30% off accounts in stores;
And for today only: 99% discount on nickname change!

The Amusement Park Awaits! Visit Marcus to learn more about the games: the Classic Duel, Blind Largus' Puzzle, and the Festive Tournament, as well as to collect a limited number of tokens for participation each day!
Additional tokens are awarded for completing quests or can be purchased in unlimited quantities for Personalized Coins from the Park Trading Store, along with other elixirs used in attractions.

The amusement attractions will be counted in the rankings, the results of which will be tallied twice: on April 21st and April 28th at 5:30. The ranking does not count toward the “Race Participant” medal line, but taking part in the attractions will allow you to unlock achievements in the "Theme Park regular” lines.

Use Jubilee Thalers in the Prize Store to exchange for rare items, including inlaid stones: Hydirite and ArAlgide, Adaliants and ArAdaliants, as well as the new items:
- Fragile Symbols, which allow you to obtain an unlearned symbol for 30 days;
- Ghostly Card of Variability, whose Joker grants a daily random bonus to one of your character’s characteristics until the end of the day. The size of the bonus is also random and depends on the Joker’s color.

The amusement park will close after April 27th, while the Prize Store will remain open until the end of April 28th, after which the park gates will close until next year.

Gifts from the Elinor Bank! By purchasing crystals before April 17th inclusive, you will receive 10 Platinum Tokens as a gift for every 100 crystals in a single transaction!

Wishing you a joyful celebration!

The understanding that winter is coming brings a sense of melancholy. Even the technomagical beauties Laura and Miella have been feeling a bit down on these autumn evenings. But fear not, it's time for outlandish gifts to brighten up the spirits of the lovely charmers of Elinor!
Upon logging into the game, you'll learn that Terrus or Terragor are waiting for you to help get over the autumn blues of the knowledge seeker. To do so, you'll need to give her a gift that reminds her of summer.

To make a gift, you need to follow the conditions:
- Time for making one gift - 4 hours;
- You can pack no more than 10 items into one gift;
- The total amount of good mood in one gift should be at least 100 points.

You will find a list of gift items and the way to receive them in the quest log after talking to Laura or Miella.
You can give a mood-cheering gift no more than once every 12 hours. If desired, for a small fee in Personalized coins, you can reset this time, resetting the quest progress, and start collecting the gift again.
For each successfully made bundle of gifts, the girls will reward you with a Happy autumn chest.

After opening the chest, you will receive:
- 2-4 vials of sun rays;
- brains;
- 2 peaceful protectresses;
- 5 regular magic accumulators;
- 20 suns.

The collected bottles of sun rays can be exchanged for rewards:
- 10 vials for 2 one-time portals to Gron-Norg or a magic guiding lamp;
- 20 vials for 4 ghostly cards of Light and Darkness, 5 Technowarrior chests, or an epic rasp;
- 50 vials for 25 boxes of Light, an epic needle file or 4 fragile cornucopia;
- 100 vials for 25 autumn surprise boxes, 50 mysterious artifacts, or 250 fragments of the fractal matrix (from level 11);
- 150 vials for 6 memories of the heroes, a barrel of denial (only once), or a fragile gardener's rune.

To speed up the improvement of Laura’s and Miella's moods, the Bank of Elinor offers special gifts! Until November 12th, for every 100 crystals from the amount of one payment, you will receive 1 circle for swimming, providing an immediate 60 points of good mood!
You can heal from the blues by giving gifts until November 16th included, and receive rewards from chests and vials until the end of autumn.

Among the list of rewards for vials of sun rays, you will find ghostly cards of Light and Darkness. This means that in the world of Elinor, new card decks have appeared, forming Jokers of Light and Darkness. This will grant you the effects of the weakness of either Light or Darkness depending on the type of Joker, that is weakening the effects of pennants.
You can obtain cards randomly by winning battles in the Dark Vaults. After collecting cards of all types of pennants of Light or Darkness, you can combine them into a Joker. Then you can improve it with the help of a card box up to legendary level, thereby reducing the waiting time until the next use.
You can also randomly obtain cards of Light or Darkness from a ghostly card or exchange 3 identical cards for one random card.

We wish you a successful recovery from autumn blues!

There are a few days left before the start of the academic year and it's time to repeat what you've previously learned or start studying a couple days early to get ahead of your opponents in knowledge and brainpower!

Before the end of September 5th, all Elinorians of level 5 and higher are invited to attend preparation classes consisting of "Preparing for school" and " Tutorials" assignments (assignments are available if not previously completed), as well as the "Elinor knowledge exam". You can get exam tickets for completing daily quests or purchase those from the Crystal store after completing the previous quests and no sooner than you get level 6.

You have the chance to obtain regular or heroic personalized chests by defeating valiant enemies and monsters until the end of September 3rd. The number of normal chests you can get from monsters is limited, and you can buy an unlimited number of heroic chests at the Rarity store.
Normal chests are opened by an uncomplicated action, while heroic chests require you to pay a small amount of personalized coins to open. Among the various rewards in the chests you can get - a certificate to change the level of your character or an individual seal.

There are also technomagic promotions and discounts on various types of items in the coming days:
- throughout today your armor will not lose strength in dangerous territories in a defeat and 15% discount on crystal image enhancers for personal coins in the artifact hall;
- On August the 31st, fighting within the walls of the Colosseum, you will receive tauri: guaranteed when defeating a valiant opponent and with a chance of defeating a spirit of the Colosseum. You will also get a 30% discount on all medals on sale;
- September 1st when entering the game you will receive the master effect, which doubles the points in battle medals and achievements, and also sums up with similar effects and a 20% discount on the purchase of clan and artifact armor;
- On September 2nd, the Headman and Elder of towns will give you your choice of Denial or Omniscience effect and 20% off the purchase of clan and artifact jewelry;
- On September 3rd, in all victories over valiant opponents, you have a chance to receive a Fortune Cookie and 20% off crafting and swapping with crafting custom items in the in-game forge.

And, of course, a wide variety of themed gifts awaits you at the counters of the town's florists.

Congratulations on the upcoming Knowledge Day!

This weekend will bring another surprise for technomagicians with another sale on useful items and Lottery Ticket #10. 

Until the end of the weekend, there will be sale on items and services: 
[list]
[*] 50% off the purchase of artifact armor, weapons and jewelry; 
[*] 20% on all inlaid stones available for purchase for prize tokens and tauri; 
[*] 20% on all items for gold lenses; 
[*] 30% on valor earrings boxes for tauri; 
[*] 40% on all items with fixture type.
[/list]
The Elinor Bank is presenting ticket #10 of the draw as a gift. [b]For every 500 crystals of one payment you receive 1 lottery ticket[/b]. The prizes include a magical hermit's chest, a money tree fruit leaf or 50 personalized coins and new items, an enchanted safe box and an additional safe box! 
The extra safe cell increases the capacity of the optical safe by 50%, and the enchanted safe cell will make the optical safe dimensionless. Note that only one safe will work at a time.

[i]Good shopping and great prizes![/i]

Snow and cold are on the way, which means it's a good time to start thinking about getting ready for winter and start gathering warm clothing for the residents! 
In the near future, you'll be collecting fabrics and leather to sew frost-resistant garments and maybe you'll be able to achieve the title of "Great Tailor", unless you've received it before!
You will need a special pattern from a merchant near the Colosseum and the following materials to make the clothes: 
[list]
[*] Dressed fur. With a chance you can get it when defeating bats, bloodsuckers, caveman, rat, bear, vampire, kobold, vugluskr and goblins of the Hive.
[*] Durable Skin. With a chance is found in the reward from monsters: lizard, varan, drake, worm, octopulus, lizardfish, blind, infected goblin, and gravedigger.
[*] Soft Fluff. With a small chance is dropped from spirit, ghost, spectre, gander, phantom, Colosseum spirits, stellar, and luminary.
[*] Spider thread. Sometimes it is dropped from an arachnid:adult spider, darkworm, and black arachnid.
[*] Roll of fabric. Can be earned by opening troll bags. 
[/list]
You will also need a tailor's kit. It includes: 2 iron ore, 10 linen threads, 2 sets of needles, and a measuring tape, which can be received from a defeated opponent of an enemy faction. You can buy the measuring tape at the Crystal store if you want. 

When you ship finished items to warehouse of the Elinor, you will receive one point toward the "Great tailor" achievement and a randomly generated gift:
[list]
[*] Pouch of weakening platum fragments;
[*] 10 sunnies;
[*] Fortune token;
[*] Magic heroic, epic or legendary crystal;
[*] 10 crystals of hatred by level;
[*] 6 heavenly pearls;
[*] 2 combat cobblestones;
[*] 3 Khatog or Longholm fighter packs;
[*] Tripled points in the Great tailor achievement;
[*] 4 сrystals of depletion.
[/list]
You must supply at least 1000 frostproof clothing to earn the achievement, and will be rewarded with a crystal of water or fire magic for 30 days as a reward. 

Players from level 6 up until and including November 27 will be able to join the "Great tailor" event.

Lucky technomagicians until the end of November 20 by defeating experienced monsters and valiant warriors will be able to get the safes of the Grobft family with some chance! There are various gifts waiting for you inside the safe. You can see the full list of rewards here, and we will write about small changes among the received gifts: in the iron safe instead of silver coins you can get a small amount of tauri, and when you open the gold safe instead of the Hive chest you will receive a ghost card!

News for "Triumph" clan ranking members: By your request, inlaid stones for tauri have appeared in the city clan stores. These two upgraded stones are quality zetheriz and arZermite. The effectiveness of these stones is 2.5 units higher than the usual ones, and they also make the item inaccessible when inserted into an item. 

And another gift from Elinor Bank: until the end of November 17, you will receive one additional techno-warrior chest for every 100 crystals of the amount of one payment.

[i]We wish you a warm winter![/i]
